# Both current upstreams (SL Transport and SL Deviations) are keyless public APIs.
# No API key is required to run this backend. It exists so that:
#  - local dev / Vercel config has one documented place for runtime env vars
#  - a future keyed upstream has an obvious place to be added without guessing the
#    variable name.
#
# The Upstash Redis credentials below are the one real secret this backend has today.
# NEVER commit real values here — this file only ever holds placeholders/comments; real
# credentials belong in Vercel's own Environment Variables settings (or a local,
# git-ignored .env file) and nowhere else.

# Port used only by the local Node dev server (src/server.ts). Ignored on Vercel.
PORT=8787

# "development" | "production" | "test"
NODE_ENV=development

# Overridable upstream base URLs (defaults match the documented production endpoints).
# SL_TRANSPORT_BASE_URL=https://transport.integration.sl.se/v1
# SL_DEVIATIONS_BASE_URL=https://deviations.integration.sl.se/v1
# SL_JOURNEY_PLANNER_BASE_URL=https://journeyplanner.integration.sl.se/v2

# How long (ms) to wait for an upstream response before aborting and returning
# UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT (504). Default: 10000 (10s). See src/lib/upstreamFetch.ts.
# UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT_MS=10000

# Upstash Redis REST credentials — the shared cache/distributed lock that protects the
# SL Deviations upstream across every Vercel instance (see docs/api-contract.md,
# "Caching and fair use", and src/services/deviationsSnapshotService.ts). These are the
# exact variable names Vercel's own Upstash marketplace integration populates
# automatically once a Redis database is connected to the project — no renaming needed
# there.
#
# REQUIRED in production (NODE_ENV=production): the backend refuses to start without
# both set (see src/config/env.ts, readRedisConfig) — production must never silently
# fall back to the per-instance in-memory cache/lock, which provides no cross-instance
# protection at all against SL's "at most one request per minute" fair-use limit.
#
# Optional in local development and tests: when both are left unset, the in-memory
# implementations are used instead (correct for local dev and for the automated test
# suite — see src/lib/cache.ts / src/lib/distributedLock.ts).
#
# Get these from an Upstash Redis database (upstash.com), or via Vercel's own Storage
# tab → Upstash integration, which creates the database and sets both automatically.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-database.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=your-upstash-rest-token
# Google Play purchase verification. Keep the private key only in local/Vercel secrets.
# GOOGLE_PLAY_PACKAGE_NAME=se.blick.app
# GOOGLE_PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=blick-play-verifier@your-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com
# GOOGLE_PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"
